      <h1 class="app-detail-title">Pricing</h1>
      <p class="app-detail-tagline">Free to start. One subscription for everything else.</p>

      <div class="app-detail-content">
        <section class="app-section">
          <h2 class="section-title">Free</h2>
          <p class="app-detail-description"><strong>The server and the apps cost nothing.</strong> Run Orbit on your own hardware, browse your library, and play your music at home.</p>
          <ul class="feature-list">
            <li>Self-hosted server (Docker, Linux, macOS, Raspberry Pi)</li>
            <li>Native apps for iPhone, iPad, Mac, Apple Watch, and Apple TV</li>
            <li>Full library import and management</li>
            <li>Playback on your home network</li>
            <li>No account required</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="app-section">
          <h2 class="section-title">Orbit Pro</h2>
          <p class="app-detail-description"><strong>$2.99 / month, or $24 / year.</strong> The annual plan includes a 7-day free trial.</p>
          <ul class="feature-list">
            <li>Bit-perfect exclusive mode on macOS (USB DAC, DSD)</li>
            <li>Gapless playback, crossfade, loudness normalization</li>
            <li>Listen anywhere — encrypted remote access via Orbit Cloud</li>
            <li>Multi-zone playback and multi-server support</li>
            <li>Offline downloads on iPhone and iPad</li>
            <li>Editorial mode and CarPlay</li>
            <li>One purchase unlocks iPhone, iPad, Mac, Watch, and TV</li>
            <li>Family Sharing supported</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="app-detail-description" style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>Perfect for:</strong> Audiophiles with USB DACs, vinyl archivists, classical collectors, and anyone who wants their library with them outside the house.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="app-section">
          <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <p class="app-detail-description"><strong>What stays free?</strong></p>
          <p class="app-detail-description">Everything you need to run Orbit at home: the server, the apps, library import and management, and local playback on a single server.</p>

          <p class="app-detail-description" style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>How does the subscription work?</strong></p>
          <p class="app-detail-description">Orbit Pro is purchased through the App Store and managed from your Apple account. One subscription unlocks Pro on all your Apple devices, and you can cancel anytime.</p>

          <p class="app-detail-description" style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>What happens if I cancel?</strong></p>
          <p class="app-detail-description">Your library and all your data stay exactly where they are — on your server. Pro features lock back to the free tier; nothing is deleted.</p>

          <p class="app-detail-description" style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>Is there a free trial?</strong></p>
          <p class="app-detail-description">Yes. The annual plan starts with a 7-day free trial with all Pro features unlocked.</p>

          <p class="app-detail-description" style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>Do I need an internet connection?</strong></p>
          <p class="app-detail-description">No. Orbit runs entirely on your home network. Internet is only used for metadata lookups, and for remote listening through Orbit Cloud if you choose to enable it.</p>

          <p class="app-detail-description" style="margin-top: 1rem;"><strong>Can I use Orbit commercially?</strong></p>
          <p class="app-detail-description">Orbit is for personal, non-commercial use. Contact us for commercial licensing.</p>
        </section>

